# Module Development Guidelines

## Creating New Modules

### Module Structure
When creating a new module, follow this structure:
```
Body/{admin|public}/{ModuleName}/
├── routes.json          # Route definitions
├── Controllers/         # Controller classes
│   └── {module}.php     # Main controller
├── Models/             # Model classes
│   └── {module}.php     # Main model
└── Views/              # View templates
    └── {module}.ct      # Main view template
```

### Route Configuration
Define routes in `routes.json`:
```json
{
  "routes": [
    {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/module/action",
      "controller": "ModuleController",
      "action": "actionMethod"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Controller Development
- Extend the base Controller class from [Brain/Core/Controller.php](mdc:Brain/Core/Controller.php)
- Use dependency injection through Registry
- Implement proper error handling
- Follow RESTful conventions where appropriate

### Model Development
- Extend the base Model class from [Brain/Core/Model.php](mdc:Brain/Core/Model.php)
- Use the Database class for data operations
- Implement validation methods
- Use proper relationships between models

### View Templates
- Use `.ct` extension for view files
- Follow the framework's templating system
- Implement proper escaping for security
- Use components and layouts for reusability

### Module Registration
- Register modules in the appropriate directory structure
- Update routing configuration
- Ensure proper namespace usage
- Test module functionality thoroughly

## Best Practices

### Security
- Validate all input data
- Use framework security classes
- Implement proper authentication
- Follow CSRF protection guidelines

### Performance
- Use caching mechanisms
- Optimize database queries
- Implement proper pagination
- Use lazy loading where appropriate

### Testing
- Write unit tests for controllers and models
- Test view rendering
- Validate route configurations
- Test error handling scenarios

### Documentation
- Document all public methods
- Provide usage examples
- Update module documentation
- Include configuration instructions